# Cline Rules — dima-publishing

This is the canonical repository for the BITM330 database textbook and its
publishing platform. All agent rules live in `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/`.

## Read first

Before editing any file:

1. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) — instruction precedence and project map.
2. Read [.agents/README.md](.agents/README.md) — skills index.
3. Open the relevant skill under `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` for the task
   at hand (chapter editing, media, source import, deploy, etc.).

Do not treat `.agents/archive/` as active instructions.

## Cline-specific notes

- Slash commands listed in `AGENTS.md` (e.g. `/chapter-editor`, `/chapter-media`,
  `/book-deploy`) map to skills under `.agents/skills/`. If a slash command is
  not available in Cline, open the matching `SKILL.md` and follow it manually.
- This repo and its Google Drive sibling (`BITM330-book-drive`) share the same
  `.agents/` content via a filesystem junction on the author's machine. Edit
  only the repository copy under `C:\Users\nd115232\Documents\GitHub\dima-publishing\.agents`.
- Large image originals live outside the repo at the configured media library
  path. Do not move, delete, or overwrite them without explicit approval.

## Windows PowerShell quirks

- Avoid Bash heredocs (`python - <<'PY'`). Use a script file, `python -c`, or a
  PowerShell here-string piped to Python.
- In double-quoted strings, write `${var}:` when a variable is immediately
  followed by a colon — `$var:` parses as a scoped variable reference.
- If the terminal is stuck in a Python REPL, send `exit()` before running
  normal PowerShell commands.

## Style for student-facing content

See `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and `AGENTS.md` for the full voice guide.
Headlines:

- Undergraduate business readers, Grade 8–10 reading level.
- Prefer *use, help, show, explain, because*. Avoid *utilize, facilitate,
  demonstrate, due to the fact that*. No em dashes.
- Lines starting with `//` in Markdown are author instructions — act on them,
  then delete the line.
